{"id":"se-australia","name":"South-east Australia","country":"Australia","story":"The 2019–20 Black Summer megafires in New South Wales and Victoria.","places":["New South Wales","Victoria","Gippsland"],"lang":["en"],"bbox":[146.5,-38.0,151.0,-33.5],"grid_deg":0.1,"data_through":"2026-11-11","built_at":"2026-11-11T15:14:58+00:00","estimand":{"primary":"Hotspots per period on the Aqua MODIS scale: the number of vegetation-fire detections Aqua MODIS would have recorded (early-afternoon and post-midnight passes). Day and night are calibrated separately and added.","why_aqua":"The early-afternoon orbit is the only one observed continuously from 2002 (Aqua) through Suomi-NPP, NOAA-20 and NOAA-21. Converting VIIRS to MODIS scale discards information and is well-posed; the reverse must invent small fires MODIS never saw, so the VIIRS-scale view is marked modelled before 2012.","secondary":["Fire cell-days (0.1° cell × UTC day with ≥1 detection), Aqua scale","Hotspots on the Suomi-NPP VIIRS scale (modelled before 2012)","Persistent heat sources (kilns, flares, industry, volcanoes) harmonized separately","Raw detections — not comparable across satellite eras"],"not":"Not burned area and not a count of fires: a detection is one hot pixel in one overpass."},"method":{"confidence_filter":"drop VIIRS 'l' and MODIS confidence < 30 (no crosswalk between the two scales); sensitivity reported","static_mask":"0.01° cells where science-quality FIRMS `type` is 1–3 for ≥50% of ≥3 detections","coverage":"share of days each satellite delivered data anywhere on Earth in each period (measured, so launches, gaps and the Suomi-NPP end come from the data); below 25% a satellite is left out, otherwise counts are divided by coverage","calibration":"ratio of totals per calendar month, day and night separately, shrunk toward the pooled ratio by empirical Bayes (shrinkage strength estimated from the data). Chain: Terra→Aqua (2002–2020, bridges 2000–2002 only), Suomi-NPP→Aqua (2012–2020, pre-drift), NOAA-20→Suomi-NPP, NOAA-21→NOAA-20; chain-closure mismatch is added to the error","combination":"inverse-variance mean of the satellites observing each period (calibration error + counting noise, evaluated at the pooled mean); intervals widened so 95% of held-out months fall inside (MODIS-denial test)","comparison":"each period vs the same month/week in other complete years: median, ratio, percentile, rank — no sigma thresholds (fire counts are skewed)","weekly":"ISO-8601 weeks; weeks use their Thursday's month calibration","provisional":"periods containing near-real-time rows are provisional: FIRMS replaces NRT with standard processing after ~3 months, and the mirror keeps only one of the two, so the NRT-to-standard difference cannot be measured from it"},"calibration":{"veg_det_D":[{"sensor":"MODIS_T","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2002-08","2020-12"],"beta":[2.3243,1.9458,6.4527,6.9589,6.8366,9.0343,4.1606,3.2974,2.5119,2.419,1.6971,1.6171],"pooled":3.4126,"sigma2":0.4674,"tau2":0.3432,"n_periods":218,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_SNPP","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2012-02","2020-12"],"beta":[0.1912,0.2161,0.2206,0.2712,0.3252,0.2895,0.2043,0.1962,0.1889,0.1631,0.1983,0.2302],"pooled":0.2328,"sigma2":0.0552,"tau2":0.041,"n_periods":107,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_NOAA20","reference":"VIIRS_SNPP","window":["2018-05","2026-10"],"beta":[1.0409,0.8462,1.0958,1.003,1.0324,0.9678,1.0356,0.9781,1.0136,1.2532,0.9672,0.8751],"pooled":0.9947,"sigma2":0.0499,"tau2":0.0108,"n_periods":97,"calibrated":true},{"sensor":"VIIRS_NOAA21","reference":"VIIRS_NOAA20","window":["2024-02","2026-10"],"beta":[1.0384,1.1272,1.1352,1.0212,1.0124,1.0283,0.9812,1.0411,1.046,1.2153,0.8834,0.895],"pooled":1.0329,"sigma2":0.0379,"tau2":0.013,"n_periods":31,"calibrated":true}],"veg_det_N":[{"sensor":"MODIS_T","reference":"MODIS_A","window":["2002-08","2020-12"],"beta":[0.826,0.8539,0.4277,0.4166,0.4764,0.4597,0.4953,0.7304,0.6715,0.5597,0.6258,0.8288],"pooled":0.7749,"sigma2"